<title>USA: Diagnostic gets FDA ok to market new assays.</title>
<headline>Diagnostic gets FDA ok to market new assays.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diagnostic Products Corp Friday said it received clearance from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market 61 new allergy diagnostic assays.</p>
<p>The new assays follow clearance of 57 allergy diagnostic tests in January this year and add to Diagnotic's available assays for the AlaSTAT automated test system. The AlaSTAT system is used by clinical laboratories to help diagnose patients with allergic disease.</p>
</text>
